{
  "description": [
    "Conformance fixture of the state protocol (docs/state-protocol.md): what a client must hold after each message.",
    "Every case starts with a new client, with the state {} and no number. Its steps are, in order, one of:",
    "  full: a program_state message. delta: a program_state_update message, with the status the client gives it.",
    "  reset: the client drops its connection and its state.",
    "After each step: index is the number of the last message taken (null: none), resync whether the client",
    "asked for the whole state at this step (emit program_state), and state the state held, given when the",
    "step changes it: without one the state must be the one before, untouched.",
    "Run by test/state_client.test.cjs (layout/include/state_client.js, which the web app and the Stream Deck",
    "plugin bundle), streamdeck/test/state-client.test.ts and test/test_state_protocol.py (test/state_protocol.py)."
  ],
  "actions": {"set": ["values_changed", "type_changes", "dictionary_item_added"], "remove": ["dictionary_item_removed"]},
  "cases": [
